WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.132 --> 00:00:03.697
It turned out that Mickey was right about Coach's decision.

2
00:00:03.698 --> 00:00:11.031
As soon as Patrick arrived for the Hornets game, Coach hurried over. "Feeling better, Patrick?"

3
00:00:11.032 --> 00:00:12.016
"Yep."

4
00:00:12.017 --> 00:00:14.769
"Good. Because you're starting today."

5
00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.279
Mickey flashed Patrick a grin. "I knew it."

6
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:22.438
"Thanks. We'll see how it goes," Patrick said.

7
00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:27.837
Mickey was probably disappointed, but he wasn't showing it, not at all.

8
00:00:27.838 --> 00:00:30.729
Patrick had studied the Hornets players carefully.

9
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:37.838
So the game went well—until the fifth inning when the Hornets scored a run, and the Dragons couldn't catch up.

10
00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:41.695
At the top of the seventh inning, the Hornets were still leading.

11
00:00:41.696 --> 00:00:48.755
The first two Dragons batters got on base, but the next two struck out. Gene was up next.

12
00:00:48.756 --> 00:00:52.818
"Gene's a great baseman but a weak hitter," Patrick thought.

13
00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.815
Coach waved to Mickey.

14
00:00:54.816 --> 00:00:59.605
"Here it comes," Patrick thought. "Time to put Mickey in as pinch hitter."

15
00:00:59.606 --> 00:01:03.331
"Mickey," said Coach. "Go in to hit for Gene."

16
00:01:03.332 --> 00:01:07.006
Gene handed off the bat. "You got this, Mickey."

17
00:01:07.007 --> 00:01:13.239
"Oh well," Patrick told himself. "I won't get to finish the game, but at least I started."

18
00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.834
Still Patrick knew that Coach had made the right call.

19
00:01:16.835 --> 00:01:21.226
The team needed a hit, and Mickey was the player most likely to get one.

20
00:01:21.227 --> 00:01:24.972
"Come on, Mickey," Patrick said. "Get a hit!"

21
00:01:24.973 --> 00:01:29.321
Mickey popped a foul on the first swing.

22
00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:34.131
Patrick could see Mickey digging deep, fiercely eyeing the pitcher.

23
00:01:34.132 --> 00:01:39.905
The second pitch was fast and outside, just like Mickey liked them.

24
00:01:39.906 --> 00:01:43.954
He slammed the ball far into center field and took off.

25
00:01:43.955 --> 00:01:51.041
The crowd roared as the first and then the second Dragons runner crossed home. Mickey slid into third.

26
00:01:51.042 --> 00:01:53.815
"Safe!" cried the umpire.

27
00:01:53.816 --> 00:01:56.303
The score was 2-1.

28
00:01:56.304 --> 00:02:00.200
Buck struck out, and now the Hornets were up to bat.

29
00:02:00.201 --> 00:02:04.611
Patrick pushed his way over to Mickey as the team started to take the field.

30
00:02:04.612 --> 00:02:10.696
"Nice hit, Mickey. You were patient at the plate, and it paid off. The pitcher—"

31
00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:14.924
"Hey, Patrick!" It was Daniel. "Dell's waiting!"

32
00:02:14.925 --> 00:02:20.597
"Huh?" What was Daniel talking about? Mickey was taking over as catcher.

33
00:02:20.598 --> 00:02:27.263
Daniel grinned at Patrick's confused look. "Mickey's going to third base. You're catching for Dell.

34
00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:30.430
Coach doesn't want to mess up the rhythm you two have going."

35
00:02:30.431 --> 00:02:36.478
Patrick nodded and quickly buckled on his catching equipment.

36
00:02:36.479 --> 00:02:40.404
His nerves were thrumming—he couldn't make a mistake now.

37
00:02:40.405 --> 00:02:45.595
One run would tie the game. Two runs would cost the Dragons the game.

38
00:02:45.596 --> 00:02:51.162
Patrick squatted and swept the field with his eyes, making sure his teammates were all in position.

39
00:02:51.163 --> 00:03:02.481
The batter stepped into the box. Patrick signaled for a curve. Dell threw the strikes: one, two, three, batter out!

40
00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:10.290
The second batter had a choppy swing. He popped a foul on the first pitch.

41
00:03:10.291 --> 00:03:15.728
Patrick signaled for a changeup next. Dell threw the ball.

42
00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.807
"Strike!"

43
00:03:17.808 --> 00:03:23.708
Patrick settled into position and signaled for a fastball next. Dell threw the pitch high.

44
00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:34.110
The batter popped it out toward left field. Todd took off after the foul and caught it, smacking hard into the fence.

45
00:03:34.111 --> 00:03:38.290
"Two outs!" thought Patrick. "One more for the win!"

46
00:03:38.291 --> 00:03:42.702
Suddenly the crowd moaned.

47
00:03:42.703 --> 00:03:46.828
Patrick glanced up and saw Todd clutching his left shoulder.

48
00:03:46.829 --> 00:03:52.796
Coach met him on the field and then walked him back to the dugout.

49
00:03:52.797 --> 00:04:00.026
"Oh no," thought Patrick, exchanging glances with Dell. The two of them had just about wrapped up this game.

50
00:04:00.027 --> 00:04:08.939
Coach looked from player to player, his forehead wrinkled as he tried to decide what to do. Finally he made a decision.

51
00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:17.013
"Patrick, I think you and Dell can finish this. I'll send Pete to third base and Mickey into left field."

52
00:04:17.014 --> 00:04:23.664
Patrick reached down and rubbed his lucky mitt. Things were finally going his way.

53
00:04:23.665 --> 00:04:32.180
Then he looked at the next batter and groaned. Number 28 was a power hitter who tended to pull left.

54
00:04:32.181 --> 00:04:38.487
The Dragons had to have a strong fielder in left field. He thought for only a second before speaking up.

55
00:04:38.488 --> 00:04:39.668
"Coach?"

56
00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:41.987
Everyone was looking at Patrick.

57
00:04:41.988 --> 00:04:50.732
"This next guy is a power hitter, and he pulls left. So . . ." Patrick paused, suddenly nervous about questioning Coach's decision.

58
00:04:50.733 --> 00:04:58.134
"So I was thinking about our positions. Mickey can catch well, but I'd probably be better in left field."

59
00:04:58.135 --> 00:05:02.141
Coach frowned. "You sure about the batter's hitting, Patrick?"

60
00:05:02.142 --> 00:05:06.204
Patrick nodded. "I know the Hornets' batters pretty well."

61
00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:11.882
"Then good call," Coach said. He looked at Mickey. "Suit up. You're catching."

62
00:05:11.883 --> 00:05:16.414
Patrick unbuckled his gear.

63
00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:20.604
"Come on, Mickey," said Dell. "Let's finish this."

64
00:05:20.605 --> 00:05:26.109
As Mickey headed toward home plate, Patrick grabbed his sleeve.

65
00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:29.852
"I'd go with the changeup and a high pitch."

66
00:05:29.853 --> 00:05:32.275
Mickey nodded. "Thanks."

67
00:05:32.276 --> 00:05:38.536
Patrick trotted out to left field, hoping he hadn't steered Mickey or Coach wrong.

68
00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:42.504
He stood ready, but the batter fouled the first two pitches.

69
00:05:42.505 --> 00:05:48.009
"Hang in there, Dell," thought Patrick. "One more pitch could do it."

70
00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:55.660
But the next pitch was wild. Mickey dove to block the ball and made the recovery.

71
00:05:55.661 --> 00:06:02.905
The next two pitches were balls. Now there was a full count: the batter had two strikes and three balls.

72
00:06:02.906 --> 00:06:10.300
Patrick's heart pounded. This was it. The Dragons could win with this next play.

73
00:06:10.301 --> 00:06:13.252
But Patrick could see that Dell was tired.

74
00:06:13.253 --> 00:06:18.815
"Fastball!" Patrick thought, wishing there was some way to communicate his thought to Mickey.

75
00:06:18.816 --> 00:06:26.133
From experience, Patrick knew that Dell could throw a fastball straight down the slot, no matter how tired he was.

76
00:06:26.134 --> 00:06:34.377
Dell wound up and zipped the ball toward the catcher's mitt. The batter swung, and the ball popped straight up.

77
00:06:34.378 --> 00:06:42.729
Mickey scrambled to pull off his mask as the crowd roared. Patrick screamed with the rest of them. "Catch it!"

78
00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:47.147
Mickey spotted the ball as it sailed down toward a spot behind home plate.

79
00:06:47.148 --> 00:06:54.123
He turned and took off running. He dived under the ball and rolled.

80
00:06:54.124 --> 00:06:59.374
Patrick squeezed his eyes shut for a second. Would Mickey come up with the ball?

81
00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:03.219
Mickey raised his mitt from a cloud of dust.

82
00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:06.223
"Out!" cried the umpire.

83
00:07:06.224 --> 00:07:12.516
"Woo-hoo!" shouted Patrick. The Dragons had beaten the Hornets!

84
00:07:12.517 --> 00:07:20.516
The other players mobbed Mickey. Patrick ran in to join them.

85
00:07:20.517 --> 00:07:27.515
"Smart thinking today, Patrick," Coach said. "We're lucky to have someone who can play well in two positions.

86
00:07:27.516 --> 00:07:32.015
And maybe someday we'll have another Deboe coaching too!"

87
00:07:32.016 --> 00:07:36.438
Daniel gave him a fist bump. "Proud of you, bro."

88
00:07:36.439 --> 00:07:40.655
Patrick grinned as he went back onto the field to shake hands with the Hornets.

89
00:07:40.656 --> 00:07:45.927
Crouching behind home plate and catching pitches was one of the greatest feelings he knew.

90
00:07:45.928 --> 00:07:56.593
"But the best thing about playing baseball," he thought, "is being part of a team."

